{{#if (eq ../requirement "art-5")}}
== Requirement

The organisation does not place on the market, put into service, or use AI systems for the prohibited practices. Examples are:

* manipulative or deceptive techniques that cause significant harm
* the exploitation of the vulnerabilities of people because of their age, disability, or social or economic situation
* social scoring that leads to unfair treatment
* the prediction of criminal offences only from profiling or personality traits
* the untargeted scraping of facial images to build facial recognition databases
* emotion recognition at the workplace or in education, except for medical or safety reasons
* biometric categorisation that infers sensitive characteristics, for example race, political opinions, or sexual orientation
* real-time remote biometric identification in public spaces for law enforcement, except in the cases that the regulation allows.

The prohibitions apply from 2 February 2025.

This is a summary. See the regulation and the guidelines of the European Commission on prohibited AI practices for the exact text.

