{{#if (eq ../requirement "art-26")}}
== Requirement

A deployer of a high-risk AI system:

* uses the system according to the instructions for use of the provider
* assigns human oversight to people who have the competence, the training, and the authority
* makes sure that the input data under its control is relevant for the intended purpose
* monitors the operation of the system, and informs the provider and the authorities about serious incidents and risks
* keeps the logs that the system generates under its control for at least six months
* informs the workers and their representatives before it uses the system at the workplace
* informs the people about whom the system makes decisions, or helps to make them.

The high-risk uses are listed in Article 6 and Annex III, for example in recruitment, in the evaluation of employees, and in creditworthiness. If the organisation has no high-risk use of AI, mark this requirement out of scope with a justification. The control "Manage the AI tools in use" checks this every year.

The obligations for high-risk AI systems apply later than Articles 4 and 5. Check the current dates, because the European Commission proposed in 2025 to postpone them.

This is a summary. See the regulation for the exact text, and Article 27 for the fundamental rights impact assessment of some deployers.

