{{#if (eq ../requirement "art-50")}}
== Requirement

A deployer of AI systems:

* tells people when it uses an emotion recognition or biometric categorisation system on them
* discloses that image, audio, or video content is artificially generated or manipulated, when the content is a deep fake
* discloses that text is artificially generated or manipulated, when it publishes the text to inform the public on matters of public interest, unless a person has reviewed the text and the organisation has the editorial responsibility for it.

A provider has more obligations. For example, people are told when they interact with an AI system, such as a chatbot, and generated content is marked in a machine-readable format. These apply when the organisation offers its own AI system to others, for example a chatbot on its website.

The obligations apply from 2 August 2026.

This is a summary. See the regulation and the code of practice on the transparency of AI-generated content for the exact text.

